text.section:
Examples of reasonable identification. Except as otherwise provided in subsection (d), a description of collateral reasonably identifies the collateral if it identifies the collateral by:

specific listing;


category;


except as otherwise provided in subsection (e), a type of collateral defined in the Uniform Commercial Code;


quantity;


computational or allocational formula or procedure; or


except as otherwise provided in subsection (c), any other method, if the identity of the collateral is objectively determinable.
